{#
    The tax-province explanatory paragraph, shared by PurchaseOrder's and VendorBill's EDIT screens
    (`purchase_order_edit.html.twig`'s `#po-tax-province-note` and `bill_edit.html.twig`'s
    `#bill-tax-province-note`). Both used to hand-write the same four-branch structure with the same
    reasoning and only the noun, the freeze verb and a couple of document-specific sentences
    differing; this is the one file both now include. The caller keeps its own wrapping
    `<p id="...">` — this partial renders only the branching text inside it, so each screen's id
    stays exactly where a test already looks for it.

    Every phrase that is genuinely shared (the "no tax province on this X" paragraph and its
    "now records" / "record the address" remedy) is written once below with `documentNoun`
    substituted in. Every phrase that ISN'T identical between the two documents is
    passed in as its own parameter rather than forced to match — see the two per-document sentences
    below, and VendorBill's own `warehouseKnownButNotSavedYet` branch, which PurchaseOrder never
    reaches (a purchase order's warehouse is never known before the order itself is saved; a bill
    created from `?po=` inherits its warehouse before its own first save, which is the one shape
    of this note PurchaseOrder has no equivalent for).

    Parameters
    ----------
    documentNoun                required  'order' | 'bill'
    cannotFreezeSentence         required  "An order with taxable goods and no province cannot be
                                          issued." / "A bill with taxable goods and no province
                                          cannot be approved." — a full sentence rather than
                                          composed from a noun and a verb because "an order" /
                                          "a bill" is a grammar rule, not a substitution.
    isDraft                     required  Whether this document is still a draft. PurchaseOrder's
                                          final (no-warehouse-at-all) branch is only ever reached
                                          while brand new, so passing its own `isDraft` here is
                                          always true there and changes nothing about its output.
    hasProvince                 required  Whether the document already carries a frozen province.
    provinceDisplay              optional  The frozen value's display text (PO: a province name
                                          plus its code in parens; Bill: the bare code). Only read
                                          when `hasProvince`.
    warehouse                    optional  The document's warehouse, nullable exactly as each
                                          caller's own template variable is (PurchaseOrder's is
                                          effectively always set here; VendorBill's genuinely can be
                                          null). Drives the ", from X's address" clause and the
                                          no-province remedy's warehouse name.
    savingRetakesSentence        optional  Shown when `hasProvince` and `isDraft`.
    frozenPastDraftSentence      optional  Shown when `hasProvince` and not `isDraft`.
    warehouseKnownButNotSavedYet optional  VendorBill's own extra state: a warehouse is known (from
                                          `?po=`) but nothing has been saved yet, so there is no
                                          snapshot to have gone stale. Default false.
    notYetSavedBody              optional  Rendered only when `warehouseKnownButNotSavedYet`.
    noWarehouseSentence          optional  Shown when there is no province and no warehouse at all.
    noWarehouseRemedySentence    optional  Shown alongside it, gated by `isDraft` — see the note
                                          above on why that gate is a no-op for PurchaseOrder.
#}
{% set warehouse = warehouse|default(null) %}
{% if hasProvince %}
    Tax province: <strong>{{ provinceDisplay|default('') }}</strong>{% if warehouse %}, from {{ warehouse.name }}'s address{% endif %}.
    {% if isDraft %}
        {{ savingRetakesSentence|default('') }}
    {% else %}
        {{ frozenPastDraftSentence|default('') }}
    {% endif %}
{% elseif warehouseKnownButNotSavedYet|default(false) %}
    {{ notYetSavedBody|default('') }}
{% elseif warehouse %}
    <strong>No tax province on this {{ documentNoun }}</strong>{% if not warehouse.province %} — {{ warehouse.name }} has no province recorded{% endif %}, so taxable goods on it would compute no tax.
    {% if isDraft %}
        {% if warehouse.province %}
            <strong>{{ warehouse.name }} now records {{ warehouse.province }}</strong> — this {{ documentNoun }} was entered before that, and the province is taken from the warehouse each time the draft is saved. Save this draft again to freeze it onto the {{ documentNoun }}.
        {% else %}
            Record the address under Config &rsaquo; Warehouses, then save this draft again.
        {% endif %}
        {{ cannotFreezeSentence|default('') }}
    {% endif %}
{% else %}
    {{ noWarehouseSentence|default('') }}
    {% if isDraft %}
        {{ noWarehouseRemedySentence|default('') }}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
